    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This essay won or received an honorable mention for The Boothe Prize for excellence in first-year writing. The Boothe Prize recognizes and rewards outstanding expository and argumentative writing by undergraduate students in first-year classes that satisfy the WR 1 requirement. In each award-winning essay, student writers demonstrate clarity of argument, excellent integration of research-based evidence, and compelling prose style.\r\nShould Chess AI could be considered creative? Weaving together accounts of the history and culture of chess,\r\nthe development of artificial intelligence models, and a longstanding discussion in psychology about the nature of human creativity, this essay argues that AI chess should be considered creative. The argument  suggests more broadly how humans and AIs might work together to produce novelty that can enrich human endeavors.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
